I'm assuming you mean by atomic that a single gene controls a single
aspect of a person, whereas in reality it is more likely to be groups
of genes controlling various aspects. (I've got to brush on my genetics,
which I think will be my next reading project)

I think this assumption just simplifies the debate...

> B) How do the people on this list feel about group selection?

I'm not sure what you mean by group selection. Is it the selection
of groups of genes over time? (By your next question that's what it
sounds like)...

> Related question: could there be group selection pressures towards
> atomic genes?

As in the gradual pressure to go to a point where individual genes
control individual aspects of a species?

